From b81767a250e47ce402b505225af1840d97494ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:03:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www, httpd: WAN Ports replaces the Dual WAN tab, saving
 exactly what the stock page saves

The only place to choose the WAN port was the Dual WAN tab, and nothing
said that Auto searches several ports even with Dual WAN off. The native
Reaper_WANPorts.asp takes the tab's place (menuTree url + label, the
dualWAN gate kept; SUP redirect from Advanced_WANPort_Content.asp, which
stays unchanged; reaper_native[]): port tiles with Auto and its explainer,
the pinned port with Detect again, Dual WAN, monitoring, Load Balance rules
and the ISP profile. The apply is a field-for-field port of the stock
applyRule(); a mock parity harness (28 scenarios incl. refusals) shows the
same nvram changes. One deliberate difference: a legacy single-WAN "lan" on
the combo port shows that port instead of silently selecting Auto.
JSON hooks are read as literals and free text through nvram_char_to_ascii
(ej_get_ethernet_wan_list ends in a newline; nvram_get passes ' raw).
RWAN_1..22 in all 25 packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
