+     probes several ports even with Dual WAN off - under a page named for two connections.
+     This page puts that decision first, says what Auto does (and that Reaper pins the port
+     it finds, rc/reaper_wanpin.c), then offers Dual WAN, connection monitoring and the
+     load-balance rules with every stock function.
+     THE APPLY IS THE STOCK ONE. buildPost() is a line-for-line port of the stock page's
+     applyRule() (plus initial()/form_show()/changeWANProto() for the defaults it relies on),
+     run over a plain state object instead of the stock DOM: the same nvram names, values,
+     confirmations and the same reboot. build-scripts/tests/test_wanports_parity drives the
+     stock page and this one through the same scenarios on the mock router and requires the
+     same nvram changes; keep the two in step if either moves. -->
